{
  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md Section 17 (0x1300-0x1338) per-field bit tables, cited by contract ID, and RCA-DFC-ARCH-002.md's dfc_rtl020_control_t/status_t Appendix B tables. Covers all 15 real UART registers -- REG-002's own block header (Section 17) and Section 6 Address-Map Summary both say 15, and the block lists exactly 15 rows (confirmed by direct count); RTL-020_RevA.md's own stale '11 registers' claim is wrong (missing UART_RX_OVERFLOW_COUNT/UART_RX_UNDERFLOW_COUNT/UART_TX_REJECTED_COUNT/UART_TX_UNDERFLOW_COUNT entirely), disclosed in OPEN_ISSUES.md, not followed. One real gap found and fixed while building this field map (the 12th real instance of the exact gap class already fixed for RTL-002 through RTL-019, approved before this session's edit): RTL020_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS.EVENT_OVERFLOW had no clear-forwarding control field at all in dfc_rtl020_control_t as ARCH-002 originally defined it. Fixed the same way as every prior instance: ARCH-002 grew dfc_rtl020_control_t 215->216 bits, adding rtl020_evt_overflow_status__event_overflow as a new clear_mask field at the new highest bit (215) -- every pre-existing field's bit position confirmed unchanged by direct comparison against the already-generated include/dfc_types_pkg.sv before this edit. See OPEN_ISSUES.md for the full disclosure. UART_RX_LEVEL/UART_RX_DATA/UART_TX_LEVEL are pure-RO registers (readback class 'internal_reg'/'zero' not needed -- status_registers entries only, no control_registers entry, same precedent as CAN_RX_LEVEL/CAN_RX_ID/etc. in rtl019_field_map.json). UART_BAUD_DIV/UART_TX_DATA are plain RW staging registers (status_registers entry not needed -- the generic regbank already stores and returns their written value directly, same precedent as CAN_BIT_TIMING/CAN_TX_DATA_LO_STAGE/etc.).",
